@echasnovski 

Look at this example:

https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/2a00797b-cdff-4d8a-b8f6-5dffc65c9506

I did `ci{` and instead of cutting the `{}` that's in the current line it deleted the one that is covering

I would have expected this:

```typescript
async function fetchProps() {
  const data = await db.select({ count: count() }).from(Registro).then(takeUniqueOrThrow),

  return {|};
}

```

or even better, this:

```typescript
async function fetchProps() {
  const data = await db.select({ count: count() }).from(Registro).then(takeUniqueOrThrow),

  return {
    |
  };
}

```
Instead I get this:
```typescript
async function fetchProps() {
    |
}

```
